# ============================================================================
# Damco SEO Agent System — schedule
#
# Install:
#   crontab cron/crontab          # replaces the current user's crontab
#   crontab -l                    # verify
#
# Every line assumes the repo is at /opt/damco-seo-agents and the venv at
# /opt/damco-seo-agents/.venv. Change REPO below if not.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# Nothing was scheduled. Every row in `agent_runs` was launched by hand, which
# is why six agents were overdue against their own declared cadence and the
# technical_seo data was eleven weeks old. An agent with a cadence and no
# scheduler is a documentation claim, not a behaviour.
#
# Check the result rather than trusting this file:
#   python -m common.agents          # last run + status + overdue flags
#
# Ordering matters
# ----------------
# Some agents consume another's output in the same window:
#   rank_tracker        -> gap_analyzer, event_digest   (SERP data + events)
#   sitemap_validator   -> site_auditor                 (populates `pages`)
#   backlink_analyzer   -> platform_finder              (competitor_backlinks)
# The times below leave a gap after each producer. They are not chained — a
# producer failure leaves the consumer running on the previous cycle's data,
# which is the right trade for a nightly batch. `agent_runs` records both.
#
# Cost
# ----
# rank_tracker is the only expensive job: ~$0.00465 per keyword on the standard
# queue. At 2,126 keywords that is ~$9.90 per full run, so the fortnightly
# cadence below is ~$20/month. It only queries keywords whose last snapshot is
# older than `keywords.snapshot_frequency_days`, so a run mid-cycle is cheap.
# Everything else here is free or fractions of a cent.
# ============================================================================

SHELL=/bin/bash
REPO=/opt/damco-seo-agents
PY=/opt/damco-seo-agents/.venv/bin/python
MAILTO=""

# Keep a log per agent. Rotate with logrotate; these grow slowly.
# Format: cd first so relative paths and .env resolve.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Daily — cheap, and the freshness the dashboard leans on
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Trend discovery. Free feeds + one Keyword Planner batch (~$0.05).
15 2 * * *   cd $REPO && $PY -m keyword_intelligence.trend_scout >> logs/trend_scout.log 2>&1

# GA4 behaviour metrics. Free, quota'd per property. Runs daily because the
# dashboard's conversion tiles are the ones people refresh; the window itself
# is 28 days rolling, so a missed day costs nothing. Skips cleanly when
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID is unset.
45 2 * * *   cd $REPO && $PY -m keyword_intelligence.ga4_sync >> logs/ga4_sync.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weekly
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Competitor page diffs. Free (HTTP only).
# NOTE: the first run after the content-hash change re-baselines and will
# report unusually few changes. That is correct — see migration 016.
30 2 * * 1   cd $REPO && $PY -m competitive_intelligence.competitor_monitor >> logs/competitor_monitor.log 2>&1

# Competitor publishing (sitemap diffs). Free.
30 3 * * 1   cd $REPO && $PY -m competitive_intelligence.content_monitor >> logs/content_monitor.log 2>&1

# Core Web Vitals. PageSpeed API, free tier is generous.
0 4 * * 2    cd $REPO && $PY -m technical_seo.cwv_monitor >> logs/cwv_monitor.log 2>&1

# Weekly digest of SERP events. Runs after the Monday monitors so its
# per-competitor rollup can correlate SERP movement with publishing.
0 8 * * 1    cd $REPO && $PY -m competitive_intelligence.event_digest >> logs/event_digest.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fortnightly — the paid one, plus the technical sweep
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Rank tracking. THE COST CENTRE (~$9.90 full run). Chains GSC enrichment
# automatically unless --skip-gsc. 1st and 15th at 01:00.
0 1 1,15 * * cd $REPO && $PY -m keyword_intelligence.rank_tracker >> logs/rank_tracker.log 2>&1

# Gap analysis, after rank_tracker has landed its data.
0 6 1,15 * * cd $REPO && $PY -m competitive_intelligence.gap_analyzer >> logs/gap_analyzer.log 2>&1

# Sitemap validation populates `pages`; the auditor reads it. Two hours apart.
0 1 2,16 * * cd $REPO && $PY -m technical_seo.sitemap_validator >> logs/sitemap_validator.log 2>&1
0 3 2,16 * * cd $REPO && $PY -m technical_seo.site_auditor >> logs/site_auditor.log 2>&1

# Internal link graph. Crawls the full scope every run — no cadence filter.
0 5 2,16 * * cd $REPO && $PY -m technical_seo.internal_link_analyzer >> logs/internal_link_analyzer.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monthly
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Glossary gaps and content-calendar concentration. Both free, both advisory.
0 7 3 * *    cd $REPO && $PY -m content_operations.glossary_detector >> logs/glossary_detector.log 2>&1
30 7 3 * *   cd $REPO && $PY -m content_operations.concentration_checker >> logs/concentration_checker.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOCKED — uncomment when the DataForSEO Backlinks subscription is active
#
# platform_finder depends on backlink_analyzer having populated
# competitor_backlinks, so the order below matters. vendor_scorer only has
# something to score once outreach activity exists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 0 2 4 * *    cd $REPO && $PY -m competitive_intelligence.backlink_analyzer >> logs/backlink_analyzer.log 2>&1
# 0 4 4 * *    cd $REPO && $PY -m offpage_links.backlink_tracker >> logs/backlink_tracker.log 2>&1
# 0 6 4 * *    cd $REPO && $PY -m offpage_links.platform_finder >> logs/platform_finder.log 2>&1
# 0 8 4 * *    cd $REPO && $PY -m offpage_links.vendor_scorer >> logs/vendor_scorer.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT scheduled, deliberately
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# keyword_intelligence.reports          run on demand — it is a renderer
# content_operations.brief_generator    a human picks the keywords
# content_operations.compliance_checker needs a submitted draft URL
# offpage_links.outreach_drafter        drafts are human-gated
# offpage_links.guest_post_drafter      drafts are human-gated
